1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:08,620
Every September, the hills around our
village turn gold with Meskel flowers.

2
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:16,410
Grandmother would rise at dawn and
climb the hill with her basket.

3
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:24,070
She picked a handful, but she
always set one flower apart.

4
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:31,320
That one was for her son, who had left
for Addis Ababa and rarely came home.

5
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:40,970
She pressed it between the
pages of her old Bible.

6
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:49,530
When the Demera bonfire burned,
she prayed quietly for him.

7
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:59,690
Years later, when we opened the book,
we found thirty pressed flowers.

8
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:07,220
She never forgot a single
September. Neither will we.
